ShapeLogic is a fork of BurrTools, the designer and solver for interlocking
(burr) puzzles, and is built on the work of its authors. The algorithms it
ports were written by the authors of BurrTools:

Andreas Röver (original author, 2003-2011)

With thanks, from the original AUTHORS file, to Bill Cutler, André van Kamen
and Don E. Knuth (algorithms), Ronald Kint-Bruynseels (feedback, icons,
documentation), Dic Sonneveld (burr growing), Derek Bosch (macOS binary, STL
export), Markus Götz (spheres grid), Lee Krasnow (rhombic grid), Volker
Grabsch (build system), and the patch contributors Derek Bosch, George Bell
and Barry Downes.

For later work on BurrTools, see the git history of the original repository.

The web front end is built on Girish Sharma's mockup of a BurrTools web
GUI: its design, and its HTML, CSS and interaction code, which the front end
takes over and reworks (docs/mockup/index.html, from the gh-pages branch of
https://github.com/grssam/burr-tools, commit d7afb3ed, GPL-3.0).
